diff --git a/ARCHITECTURE.md b/ARCHITECTURE.md
index 39fbffe..524ddd9 100644
--- a/ARCHITECTURE.md
+++ b/ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -130,6 +130,7 @@ Exact versions are pinned in the workspace `Cargo.toml` and `Cargo.lock` is comm
 - One writer connection (SQLite allows a single writer); a pool of read-only connections (`query_only`). `storage::Database` holds both and each storage function picks one, so the layers above never do. The writer is a sqlx pool capped at one connection: its FIFO acquisition is the write queue, so no dedicated task is needed. A transaction holds the writer until it ends, so it must never await another write. Writes are short transactions; message fan-out happens after commit. Message sends are also serialized, by a per-process lock held from id generation to `MESSAGE_CREATE` publication, so messages commit and reach gateways in id order and an `after` cursor never skips one.
 - Migrations are embedded in the binary and run at startup. Before applying a migration, the server writes a consistent snapshot with `VACUUM INTO backups/pre-migration-<version>.db`.
 - Avatars and banners share that store: each version has its own id (and a still first frame when animated), served immutable at `/api/v1/profile-images/{id}` ([ADR-0021](docs/adr/0021-compress-images-losslessly-after-upload.md)). Guild and channel icons too, at `/api/v1/icons/{id}`, but only to members of their guild (and, for a channel's icon, to those who can view the channel): uploaded with an optional square crop (centred by default), stored small (guilds 256 px, may be animated; channels 96 px, always still). Custom emoji pictures are guild images too, served the same way ([ADR-0028](docs/adr/0028-custom-emoji.md)). Pictures are compressed "visually lossless" ([ADR-0033](docs/adr/0033-visually-lossless-image-compression.md)): each is stored as the smallest of AVIF, lossless WebP or (for a photo) its stripped JPEG that keeps a SSIMULACRA2 score of 80, animations as lossy or lossless animated WebP; avatars (256 px), banners (at most 960 × 384, the middle band the card shows), icons and emoji while uploading, attachments up to 16 MP in the background after it, replacing the uploaded file and its name's extension unless its colours would change (CMYK or grey profiles, colours outside Display P3). Their type is read back from the stored bytes when served. The same job stores a smaller preview of each picture attachment larger than 800 × 600 (twice the message list's 400 × 300 box), in its own sealed file with the same quality check; the message list loads it from `/api/v1/attachments/{id}/preview` (same permission check, headers and `ETag` scheme as the attachment, which it serves itself when there is no preview), and the link opens the full file. Previews go with their attachment's row and are swept with it.
+- Audio attachments are transcoded to Ogg Opus by the same background worker ([ADR-0045](docs/adr/0045-audio-attachments-transcoded-to-opus.md)): WAV and FLAC always, MP3, AAC and M4A only above 160 kbit/s on average; symphonia decodes (pure Rust), rubato resamples to 48 kHz, libopus (built from source, linked statically) encodes 96 kbit/s stereo or 64 kbit/s mono, packet by packet, so memory follows the output. At most 2 hours of audio and 120 s per job; the result replaces the file (`audio/ogg`, name ending in `.opus`) only when strictly smaller, with no original kept and no tags carried over. More than two channels, Ogg uploads and lower bitrates stay as uploaded.
 - Attachments are stored encrypted on disk under `attachments/<shard>/<id>`, the shard being the top byte of the id mixed by SplitMix64 in hex ([ADR-0034](docs/adr/0034-shard-attachment-files-by-a-mixed-id.md); files from before are moved at startup and found in their old place until then), the id being the attachment's own until its file is recompressed: a recompressed file is written under a new id (`attachments.file_id`), the row switched to it in one transaction, and the old file deleted after the commit, so files never change in place. Pictures stored before ADR-0033 are recompressed only when an administrator runs `mellow-server admin recompress-images --confirm` after a backup; the attachment worker then takes them one at a time when no upload waits, resumable through a per-row `compression_version`. Metadata (owner, name, mime type, size, plaintext SHA-256 for deduplication) lives in SQLite. Size limits are configurable.
 - Message search uses an external-content FTS5 table, `messages_fts` (migration 0021, [ADR-0029](docs/adr/0029-message-search.md)), inside the encrypted database: tokenizer `unicode61 remove_diacritics 2`, 2- and 3-character prefix indexes, `secure-delete` on, kept in step by triggers on `messages` within the writing transaction; the same migration indexes `messages (author_id, id)` for `from:`. Every connection keeps a 32 MiB page cache, since SQLCipher decrypts each page read from disk.
 
